course: dictionary
lesson: 847
title: Bestow: giving with honour
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Bestow is a formal word, so it often shows up in stories, speeches and ceremonies. The context helps you find its meaning. «The book calls this the last best gift that the kindly demi-god is careful to bestow.» A demi-god is a half-god, and a careful, kind god is giving something special. Bestow must mean give.
explain: Check by swapping in a simpler word. «The kindly demi-god is careful to give» still makes sense, so bestow means give. The difference is that bestow is used for giving something grand, such as an honour, a gift or a title, not for passing someone a biscuit.
explain: You will meet bestow in fairy tales, where a fairy bestows a gift on a baby, and in awards, where a title or honour is bestowed on someone. When you see bestow, think give, then ask: is it a special or formal kind of giving?
fact: Bestow is a verb, which means it describes an action. Its forms are bestow, bestows, bestowed and bestowing.
fact: «Bestow» means to give something to someone, especially an honour, gift or title.
fact: Bestow is a formal word, so it is more common in books, speeches and ceremonies than in everyday talk.
fact: In fairy tales, a fairy may bestow a gift on a baby.
fact: Some religious language uses bestow, for example: God bestows blessings, as Christians believe.
exercise: The queen will bestow a medal on the brave girl. What does bestow mean? | Hide | Throw | Take away | *Give
exercise: The fairy bestowed a gift on the baby. Find and copy the word that is a form of bestow. | baby | fairy | gift | *bestowed
exercise: «The kindly demi-god» is a phrase from a book. What is a demi-god? | *A half-god | A giant with a crown | A king who rules the sea | A god who is kind to children
test: The school will bestow an award on Maya for her kindness. Which word could replace bestow without changing the meaning? | Wrap | Break | Hide | *Give
test: Which word is the past tense of bestow? | bestows | *bestowed | bestowing | bestow
exam: «the last best gift that the kindly demi-god is careful to bestow» Which word could replace bestow without changing the meaning? | Hide | Take | Wrap | *Give
